      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The Taj Mahal was commissioned by Mughal emperor Shah Jahan in memory
    of his beloved wife Mumtaz Mahal. Construction began around 1632 in Agra, India,
    and the main mausoleum was completed during the following years, with the larger
    complex taking longer to finish. The monument is primarily built from beautiful
    white marble brought from Makrana, along with red sandstone and other decorative
    materials. The Taj Mahal is famous for its remarkable symmetry, large central
    dome, four minarets, detailed carvings, and delicate inlay work using precious
    and semi-precious stones.


    The monument stands at the northern end of a
    formal Charbagh garden, a traditional four-part garden design. Long pathways
    and water channels create a strong central axis leading the viewer toward the
    mausoleum. The reflection of the Taj Mahal in the water adds to its visual beauty
    and symmetry.


    The main structure contains the cenotaphs associated with
    Mumtaz Mahal and Shah Jahan, while their actual graves are located in a lower
    chamber. The interior is decorated with intricate marble screens, floral patterns,
    calligraphy, and stone inlay.


    The Taj Mahal is also recognized as an outstanding
    achievement of Mughal architecture, combining influences from Indian, Persian,
    Islamic, and other architectural traditions. Today, it is one of India''s most
    famous cultural landmarks and a major symbol of architectural beauty, love, craftsmanship,
    and history.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
